binwalk v3.1.0: wait for every result the workers owe before leaving the main loop

The main loop ran while the queue was non-empty OR the pool's active_count()
was non-zero. threadpool's active_count() counts only jobs a worker has
already dequeued, so on a loaded machine the loop saw an empty queue and no
active worker while the one job still sat in the pool's channel -- and left.
A second gap: a worker that sent its result and went idle between the loop's
try_recv() and its next test left that result unread. Either way the run
printed "Analyzed 0 files for N file signatures", found nothing, exited 0.

Upstream: https://github.com/ReFirmLabs/binwalk/issues/971 (open at pin time).
Applies to the pinned commit 4fdab3d464d97b68e0af9088df3f9e2e1545b21c (v3.1.0).
Carried by xos; applied by arsenal/build-arsenal-c.sh patch_src(). Drop it when
a release includes the fix.

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
